# ResonantMemoryMesh — Project Analysis

## What Is RMM?

Resonant Memory Mesh is an **associative memory kernel for AI agents** that goes beyond standard RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation). Instead of relying purely on semantic/vector similarity, RMM uses **Topological Resonance** — an energy propagation algorithm that can retrieve information through **causal chains and associative links**, even when the target information has zero semantic similarity to the query.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is not a toy. The codebase is a **production-grade, two-language system** with a Rust performance kernel, Python SDK, pluggable storage backends, and a fully defined database schema.

---

## Architecture at a Glance

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["Python SDK<br/>(rmm-core)"] --> B["PyO3 FFI Bridge"]
    B --> C["Rust Kernel<br/>(rmm-rust)"]
    C --> D["L1 Cache<br/>(DashMap)"]
    A --> E["Storage Adapters"]
    E --> F["InMemoryStorage"]
    E --> G["PostgresStorage<br/>(pgvector)"]
    A --> H["WriteBackBuffer<br/>(Sharded)"]
    H --> E
    H --> D
```

