## What Has Been Built

### 1. Rust Performance Kernel (`rmm-rust/`)

A complete, high-performance Rust crate with Python bindings via PyO3.

| File | Lines | What It Does |
|------|-------|------|
| [kernel.rs](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-rust/src/kernel.rs) | 354 | **AtomicPing BFS** — the core algorithm. Layered BFS with Rayon parallel neighbor processing, FxHashMap query-local overlay, deterministic ordering |
| [cache.rs](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-rust/src/cache.rs) | 418 | **L1 Cache** — DashMap-backed thread-safe graph store with V-LRU eviction (1M node cap), SyncThread interface, staleness monitoring |
| [models.rs](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-rust/src/models.rs) | 250 | [RustNode](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-rust/src/models.rs#17-35), [RustEdge](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-rust/src/models.rs#134-144), [InternalNode](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-rust/src/models.rs#189-198), [InternalEdge](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-rust/src/models.rs#235-240) with zero-copy UUID byte paths |
| [physics.rs](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-rust/src/physics.rs) | 154 | SIMD-friendly f32 physics: decay, accumulate, activate, inhibition, batch cosine similarity |
| [lib.rs](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-rust/src/lib.rs) | 37 | PyO3 module registration |

**Key design decisions:**
- **f32 everywhere** for SIMD auto-vectorization (2x values per cache line)
- **DashMap** for lock-free concurrent reads across cores (global cache)
- **FxHashMap** for query-local overlay (no cross-thread access needed)
- **Rayon** for parallel neighbor processing within each BFS hop
- **Release profile**: LTO enabled, `codegen-units = 1`, `opt-level = 3`
- **Rust tests** embedded for physics (decay, accumulate, clamp, inhibition, batch)

---

### 2. Python SDK (`rmm-core/`)

A clean, well-structured Python SDK wrapping the Rust kernel.

| File | Lines | What It Does |
|------|-------|------|
| [mesh.py](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-core/rmm/mesh.py) | 370 | **Mesh** class — primary SDK entry point with [query()](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-core/rmm/mesh.py#125-278), [ingest()](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-core/rmm/mesh.py#311-338), [connect()](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-core/rmm/mesh.py#339-353), [flush()](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-core/rmm/mesh.py#354-356), [close()](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-core/rmm/mesh.py#357-362). Implements Hybrid Ignition, Fault-In cold start, and Atomic Pulse |
| [buffer.py](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-core/rmm/core/buffer.py) | 173 | **WriteBackBuffer** — generic async write-back with Swap & Release pattern, 16 sharded mutexes, load shedding, retry/requeue on failure |
| [synthesizer.py](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-core/rmm/core/synthesizer.py) | 68 | **Structural Rationale** generator — formats top-3 nodes and top-2 edges with confidence indicator |
| [physics.py](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-core/rmm/core/physics.py) | 51 | Python-side physics (decay, accumulate, activate, inhibition) — mirror of Rust for fallback/testing |
| [base.py](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-core/rmm/adapters/base.py) | 61 | **BaseStorage** ABC defining the storage contract (8 abstract methods) |
| [memory.py](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-core/rmm/adapters/memory.py) | 96 | **InMemoryStorage** — brute-force cosine search, dict-based, for testing/prototyping |
| [postgres.py](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-core/rmm/adapters/postgres.py) | 222 | **PostgresStorage** — production adapter with psycopg3 C-backend, connection pooling (2-20), pgvector cosine distance, CTE batch neighbor fetch |

**Query pipeline (7 stages):**
1. Vector Search → candidate IDs
2. Hybrid Ignition → re-rank by [(similarity * α) + (significance * (1-α))](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-rust/src/kernel.rs#82-86)
3. L1 Cache check → Passive Warming (push L2 fetches to L1)
4. Fault-In → fetch missing neighbors for BFS cold start
5. Kernel propagation → Rust BFS hot path ([execute_raw](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-rust/src/kernel.rs#105-133))
6. Buffered write-back → async energy persistence
7. Rationale synthesis → structural summary

