### 3. Database Layer

| File | What It Does |
|------|------|
| [schema.sql](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-core/sql/schema.sql) | Full PostgreSQL schema: [nodes](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-rust/src/cache.rs#403-407) table with [vector(128)](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-rust/src/models.rs#100-105) pgvector column, [edges](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-rust/src/cache.rs#294-300) table with composite PK, `archived_nodes` for Sleep Cycle, IVFFlat index (with HNSW alternative commented), 3 helper functions |
| [docker-compose.yml](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-core/docker-compose.yml) | Production-tuned Postgres 15 with pgvector v0.5.0 (512MB shared_buffers, 200 max connections, WAL tuning) |

**SQL Functions implemented:**
- [upsert_nodes(JSONB)](file:///Users/affantanke/Developer/ResonantMemoryMesh/rmm-rust/src/cache.rs#262-268) — batch upsert with Last-Write-Wins
- `fetch_neighbors_batch(UUID[], min_weight, max_per_source)` — CTE with `ROW_NUMBER` partitioning
- `vector_search_cosine(vector, top_k)` — cosine distance search

